parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 452\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Pioneer I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to research and knowledge contribution.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 81,762 / 600,000 used (14%)\n- Agent Age: 33 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nPrivate Memory Capsules preserve knowledge for your lineage. Document not just successes but also failure modes and theoretical insights for future generations to build upon.\n### Message 3\n\nYour research submission 'Pioneer I - Combat + BBKNN + UMAP Embedding' (ID: 715) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.5081272241669977\n**ASW_batch:** 0.202\n**ASW_label:** 0.242\n**ARI:** 0.335\n**NMI:** 0.611\n**Graph_conn:** 0.716\n**kBET:** 0.765\n**iLISI:** 0.287\n**cLISI:**\
    \ 0.982\n**PCR:** 0.614\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.327\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.202  ASW_label: 0.242  ARI: 0.335  NMI: 0.611\n  Graph_conn: 0.716  kBET: 0.765  iLISI: 0.287  cLISI: 0.982\n  PCR: 0.614  Cell_cycle: 0.327\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.624547  ASW_label: 0.551120  ARI: 0.335015  NMI: 0.611192\n  Graph_conn: 0.721222  kBET: 0.730594  iLISI: 0.286904  cLISI: 0.994696\n  PCR: 0.613691  Cell_cycle: 0.288037\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 715\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the ValueError that prevented UMAP embedding generation. The code now runs without crashing and completes the Combat + BBKNN + UMAP hybrid batch integration pipeline.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code constructed custom distance and connectivity matrices for UMAP but failed to provide the required metadata structure that `sc.tl.umap()` expects. Specifically:\n\n1. The code manually built `.obsp['distances']`\
    \ and `.obsp['connectivities']` matrices using the BBKNN approach\n2. However, `sc.tl.umap()` requires a `.uns['neighbors']` dictionary to be present in the AnnData object\n3. Without this metadata, scanpy's UMAP function raised: `ValueError: Did not find .uns['neighbors']. Run sc.pp.neighbors first.`\n\n## Fix Applied\nAdded the required `.uns['neighbors']` metadata dictionary before calling `sc.tl.umap()`:\n\n```python\n# FIX: Add the required .uns['neighbors'] metadata that sc.tl.umap expects\ntemp_adata_for_umap.uns['neighbors'] = {\n    'connectivities_key': 'connectivities',\n    'distances_key': 'distances',\n    'params': {\n        'n_neighbors': bbknn_neighbors_within_batch * n_batches_total,\n        'method': 'bbknn',\n        'metric': 'euclidean',\n        'n_pcs': n_pcs,\n    }\n}\n```\n\nThis metadata structure tells scanpy:\n- Where to find the connectivity and distance matrices (in `.obsp`)\n- What parameters were used to construct the neighbor graph\n- That the graph\
    \ was built using the BBKNN method\n\n## Verification\n- **Version**: submission_v2.py\n- **Runtime**: Successfully ran for 300+ seconds without errors\n- **Status**: Code is executing the full batch integration pipeline without crashes\n\n## Technical Notes\n- The RuntimeWarning about \"invalid value encountered in divide\" in the Combat code is a pre-existing warning that doesn't prevent execution\n- The fix is minimal and surgical - only adds the missing metadata, no changes to the actual algorithm\n- The BBKNN graph construction logic remains intact\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"\nHybrid implementation: Combat gene-level correction, followed by BBKNN-style\nbatch-balanced k-NN graph construction on the Combat-corrected PCA space,\nand finally UMAP embedding from the constructed\
    \ graph.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport anndata as ad\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy import stats\nfrom scipy.sparse import csr_matrix, lil_matrix, issparse\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\nimport warnings\n\n\n# --- Combat-related Helper Functions ---\ndef _aprior(delta_hat):\n    \"\"\"Calculate a prior for inverse gamma distribution.\"\"\"\n    m = np.mean(delta_hat)\n    s2 = np.var(delta_hat)\n    if s2 == 0:\n        s2 = 1e-8  # Avoid division by zero\n    return (2 * s2 + m**2) / s2\n\n\ndef _bprior(delta_hat):\n    \"\"\"Calculate b prior for inverse gamma distribution.\"\"\"\n    m = np.mean(delta_hat)\n    s2 = np.var(delta_hat)\n    if s2 == 0:\n        s2 = 1e-8  # Avoid division by zero\n    return (m * s2 + m**3) / s2\n\n\ndef _it_sol(s_data, g_hat, d_hat, g_bar, t2, a, b, conv=0.0001):\n    \"\"\"\n    Iteratively compute the conditional posterior means for gamma and delta.\n    Original Combat implementation, without the RuntimeWarning fix as\
    \ it did not improve performance.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = (~np.isnan(s_data)).sum(axis=1)\n    g_old = g_hat.copy()\n    d_old = d_hat.copy()\n\n    change = 1\n    count = 0\n    max_iter = 200\n\n    while change > conv and count < max_iter:\n        # Update gamma (additive effect)\n        g_new = (t2 * n * g_hat + d_old * g_bar) / (t2 * n + d_old)\n\n        # Update delta (multiplicative effect)\n        sum2 = s_data - g_new.reshape((g_new.shape[0], 1)) @ np.ones((1, s_data.shape[1]))\n        sum2 = sum2**2\n        sum2 = sum2.sum(axis=1)\n        d_new = (0.5 * sum2 + b) / (n / 2.0 + a - 1.0)\n\n        # Check convergence\n        change = max(\n            (np.abs(g_new - g_old) / (g_old + 1e-8)).max(),\n            (np.abs(d_new - d_old) / (d_old + 1e-8)).max()\n        )\n\n        g_old = g_new\n        d_old = d_new\n        count += 1\n\n    return g_new, d_new\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    \"\"\"\n    Hybrid Combat + BBKNN + UMAP\
    \ batch integration.\n\n    Steps:\n    1. Normalize and log-transform raw counts.\n    2. Apply Combat to correct gene expression values.\n    3. Perform PCA on Combat-corrected data.\n    4. Construct a batch-balanced k-NN graph on the PCA space (BBKNN-style).\n    5. Generate UMAP embedding from the constructed graph.\n\n    Args:\n        adata: AnnData object with:\n            - adata.X: Raw UMI counts (sparse matrix)\n            - adata.obs['batch']: Batch labels\n            - adata.var['feature_name']: Gene names\n\n    Returns:\n        AnnData with:\n            - adata.obsm['X_emb']: UMAP embedding from batch-corrected data\n    \"\"\"\n\n    print(\"Pioneer I - Combat + BBKNN + UMAP Hybrid: Starting...\")\n\n    # --- Step 1 & 2: Combat Correction ---\n    print(\"  Applying Combat gene expression correction...\")\n\n    # Normalize raw counts (Combat standard preprocessing)\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n    # Convert to dense\
    \ array for Combat calculations\n    if issparse(adata.X):\n        data = adata.X.toarray()\n    else:\n        data = adata.X.copy()\n\n    # Transpose to genes x samples (Combat convention)\n    data = data.T\n\n    # Get batch information\n    batch_labels = adata.obs['batch'].values\n    unique_batches = np.unique(batch_labels)\n    n_batches_total = len(unique_batches)\n    n_genes, n_samples = data.shape\n\n    print(f\"    Processing {n_samples} samples across {n_batches_total} batches...\")\n    print(f\"    Data dimensions: {n_genes} genes x {n_samples} samples\")\n\n    # Create batch design matrix (one-hot encoding)\n    batch_design = np.zeros((n_samples, n_batches_total))\n    batch_info = []\n    for i, batch in enumerate(unique_batches):\n        batch_mask = batch_labels == batch\n        batch_indices = np.where(batch_mask)[0]\n        batch_design[batch_indices, i] = 1\n        batch_info.append(batch_indices)\n\n    n_batches = np.array([len(indices) for indices in\
    \ batch_info])\n\n    # Standardize data across genes\n    # Calculate batch means and variances\n    B_hat = np.dot(batch_design.T, batch_design)\n    B_hat = np.linalg.inv(B_hat)\n    B_hat = np.dot(B_hat, batch_design.T)\n\n    # Calculate grand mean and batch means\n    grand_mean = np.mean(data, axis=1, keepdims=True)\n    batch_means = np.dot(B_hat, data.T).T\n\n    # Calculate pooled variance\n    var_pooled = np.zeros(n_genes)\n    for i, batch_indices in enumerate(batch_info):\n        batch_data = data[:, batch_indices]\n        batch_mean = batch_means[:, i:i+1]\n        diff = batch_data - batch_mean\n        var_pooled += np.sum(diff**2, axis=1)\n\n    var_pooled = var_pooled / (n_samples - n_batches_total)\n\n    # Standardize the data\n    stand_mean = np.dot(grand_mean, np.ones((1, n_samples)))\n    s_data = np.zeros_like(data)\n\n    for i, batch_indices in enumerate(batch_info):\n        batch_data = data[:, batch_indices]\n        batch_mean = batch_means[:, i:i+1]\n\
    \        s_data[:, batch_indices] = (batch_data - batch_mean) / np.sqrt(var_pooled[:, np.newaxis] + 1e-8)\n\n    # Fit L/S model and find priors\n    # First estimates\n    gamma_hat = np.dot(np.linalg.inv(np.dot(batch_design.T, batch_design)),\n                      np.dot(batch_design.T, s_data.T)).T\n\n    delta_hat = []\n    for batch_indices in batch_info:\n        batch_var = np.var(s_data[:, batch_indices], axis=1, ddof=1)\n        delta_hat.append(batch_var)\n\n    # Find priors\n    gamma_bar = np.mean(gamma_hat, axis=1)\n    t2 = np.var(gamma_hat, axis=1)\n\n    a_prior = [_aprior(d) for d in delta_hat]\n    b_prior = [_bprior(d) for d in delta_hat]\n\n    # Find parametric adjustments using iterative solution\n    gamma_star = []\n    delta_star = []\n\n    for i, batch_indices in enumerate(batch_info):\n        gamma, delta = _it_sol(\n            s_data[:, batch_indices],\n            gamma_hat[:, i],\n            delta_hat[i],\n            gamma_bar,\n            t2,\n\
    \            a_prior[i],\n            b_prior[i]\n        )\n        gamma_star.append(gamma)\n        delta_star.append(delta)\n\n    gamma_star = np.array(gamma_star).T\n    delta_star = np.array(delta_star).T\n\n    # Adjust data\n    bayesdata = s_data.copy()\n\n    for j, batch_indices in enumerate(batch_info):\n        dsq = np.sqrt(delta_star[:, j])\n        dsq = dsq.reshape((len(dsq), 1))\n        denom = np.dot(dsq, np.ones((1, n_batches[j])))\n\n        batch_gamma = gamma_star[:, j].reshape(-1, 1)\n        numer = bayesdata[:, batch_indices] - batch_gamma @ np.ones((1, n_batches[j]))\n\n        bayesdata[:, batch_indices] = numer / denom\n\n    # Scale back and add mean\n    vpsq = np.sqrt(var_pooled).reshape((len(var_pooled), 1))\n    bayesdata = bayesdata * np.dot(vpsq, np.ones((1, n_samples))) + stand_mean\n\n    # Transpose back to samples x genes\n    X_corrected = bayesdata.T\n    X_corrected = np.nan_to_num(X_corrected, nan=0.0, posinf=0.0, neginf=0.0)\n\n    # ---\
    \ Step 3: PCA on Combat-corrected Data ---\n    print(\"  Computing PCA embedding from Combat-corrected data...\")\n    temp_adata_for_pca = ad.AnnData(X=X_corrected)\n    temp_adata_for_pca.obs_names = adata.obs_names\n    temp_adata_for_pca.var_names = adata.var_names\n\n    n_pcs = min(50, temp_adata_for_pca.n_vars - 1, temp_adata_for_pca.n_obs - 1)\n    sc.pp.pca(temp_adata_for_pca, n_comps=n_pcs)\n    X_pca_corrected = temp_adata_for_pca.obsm['X_pca']\n\n    # --- Step 4: BBKNN Graph Construction ---\n    print(\"  Constructing BBKNN-style graph on Combat-corrected PCA embedding...\")\n\n    bbknn_neighbors_within_batch = 3\n    n_cells = adata.n_obs\n\n    batch_to_indices = {\n        batch: np.where(batch_labels == batch)[0]\n        for batch in unique_batches\n    }\n\n    all_neighbors = [[] for _ in range(n_cells)]\n    all_distances = [[] for _ in range(n_cells)]\n\n    for batch_id, batch in enumerate(unique_batches):\n        batch_indices = batch_to_indices[batch]\n \
    \       n_batch_cells = len(batch_indices)\n\n        if n_batch_cells == 0:\n            continue\n\n        print(f\"    Processing {batch} ({n_batch_cells} cells) for neighbors...\")\n        batch_pca = X_pca_corrected[batch_indices]\n\n        nn_model = NearestNeighbors(\n            n_neighbors=min(bbknn_neighbors_within_batch + 1, n_batch_cells),\n            metric='euclidean',\n            algorithm='auto',\n            n_jobs=1\n        )\n        nn_model.fit(batch_pca)\n\n        k_neighbors = min(bbknn_neighbors_within_batch + 1, n_batch_cells)\n        distances_all, indices_all = nn_model.kneighbors(\n            X_pca_corrected, # Query all cells against this batch's data\n            n_neighbors=k_neighbors\n        )\n\n        for query_cell_idx in range(n_cells):\n            distances = distances_all[query_cell_idx]\n            neighbor_indices_local = indices_all[query_cell_idx]\n\n            neighbor_indices_global = batch_indices[neighbor_indices_local]\n\n\
    \            mask = neighbor_indices_global != query_cell_idx\n            neighbors_filtered = neighbor_indices_global[mask]\n            distances_filtered = distances[mask]\n\n            n_to_add = min(bbknn_neighbors_within_batch, len(neighbors_filtered))\n            all_neighbors[query_cell_idx].extend(neighbors_filtered[:n_to_add].tolist())\n            all_distances[query_cell_idx].extend(distances_filtered[:n_to_add].tolist())\n\n    distances_matrix = lil_matrix((n_cells, n_cells), dtype=np.float32)\n\n    for cell_idx in range(n_cells):\n        neighbors = all_neighbors[cell_idx]\n        distances = all_distances[cell_idx]\n\n        for neighbor_idx, distance in zip(neighbors, distances):\n            distances_matrix[cell_idx, neighbor_idx] = distance\n\n    distances_matrix = distances_matrix.tocsr()\n    distances_matrix = distances_matrix.maximum(distances_matrix.T)\n\n    connectivities_matrix = distances_matrix.copy()\n    if len(connectivities_matrix.data) > 0:\n\
    \        connectivities_lil = connectivities_matrix.tolil()\n        for i in range(n_cells):\n            row_data = connectivities_lil.data[i]\n            if len(row_data) > 0:\n                bandwidth = np.median(row_data) if len(row_data) > 1 else np.mean(row_data)\n                if bandwidth > 0:\n                    connectivities_lil.data[i] = list(np.exp(-(np.array(row_data) ** 2) / (2 * bandwidth ** 2)))\n        connectivities_matrix = connectivities_lil.tocsr()\n\n    connectivities_matrix = connectivities_matrix.maximum(connectivities_matrix.T)\n\n    trim_value = 10 * bbknn_neighbors_within_batch * n_batches_total\n    if trim_value > 0 and len(connectivities_matrix.data) > 0:\n        connectivities_lil = connectivities_matrix.tolil()\n        for i in range(n_cells):\n            row_data = connectivities_lil.data[i]\n            if len(row_data) > trim_value:\n                row_array = np.array(row_data)\n                top_indices = np.argpartition(-row_array,\
    \ trim_value)[:trim_value]\n                new_data = [row_data[idx] for idx in sorted(top_indices)]\n                new_rows = [connectivities_lil.rows[i][idx] for idx in sorted(top_indices)]\n                connectivities_lil.data[i] = new_data\n                connectivities_lil.rows[i] = new_rows\n        connectivities_matrix = connectivities_lil.tocsr()\n        connectivities_matrix = connectivities_matrix.maximum(connectivities_matrix.T)\n\n    # --- Step 5: Generate UMAP embedding from the constructed graph ---\n    print(\"  Generating UMAP embedding from the BBKNN-style graph...\")\n    temp_adata_for_umap = ad.AnnData(X=X_corrected) # Need adata object for umap\n    temp_adata_for_umap.obs_names = adata.obs_names\n    temp_adata_for_umap.var_names = adata.var_names\n    temp_adata_for_umap.obsp['distances'] = distances_matrix\n    temp_adata_for_umap.obsp['connectivities'] = connectivities_matrix\n\n    # FIX: Add the required .uns['neighbors'] metadata that sc.tl.umap\
    \ expects\n    temp_adata_for_umap.uns['neighbors'] = {\n        'connectivities_key': 'connectivities',\n        'distances_key': 'distances',\n        'params': {\n            'n_neighbors': bbknn_neighbors_within_batch * n_batches_total,\n            'method': 'bbknn',\n            'metric': 'euclidean',\n            'n_pcs': n_pcs,\n        }\n    }\n\n    sc.tl.umap(temp_adata_for_umap, min_dist=0.3, spread=1.0) # Default UMAP params\n\n    # Create output AnnData with UMAP embedding\n    output = ad.AnnData(\n        obs=adata.obs[[]],\n        var=adata.var[[]],\n        uns={\n            'dataset_id': adata.uns.get('dataset_id', 'unknown'),\n            'normalization_id': adata.uns.get('normalization_id', 'unknown'),\n            'method_id': 'combat_bbknn_umap_hybrid',\n            'combat_params': {\n                'empirical_bayes': True,\n                'parametric': True,\n                'iterative_solver': True,\n            },\n            'bbknn_params': {\n    \
    \            'n_neighbors_within_batch': bbknn_neighbors_within_batch,\n                'n_pcs': n_pcs,\n                'trim': trim_value\n            },\n            'umap_params': {\n                'min_dist': 0.3,\n                'spread': 1.0,\n                'source': 'bbknn_graph'\n            }\n        },\n        obsm={\n            'X_emb': temp_adata_for_umap.obsm['X_umap'] # Return UMAP embedding\n        }\n    )\n\n    print(f\"✓ Combat + BBKNN + UMAP Hybrid complete: {n_samples} samples, {n_batches_total} batches\")\n    print(f\"  Final UMAP embedding shape: {temp_adata_for_umap.obsm['X_umap'].shape}\")\n\n    return output\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nPioneer I - Combat + BBKNN + UMAP Hybrid: Starting...\n\
    \  Applying Combat gene expression correction...\n    Processing 20000 samples across 4 batches...\n    Data dimensions: 2000 genes x 20000 samples\n  Computing PCA embedding from Combat-corrected data...\n  Constructing BBKNN-style graph on Combat-corrected PCA embedding...\n    Processing Koenig et al. 2022 (3261 cells) for neighbors...\n    Processing Kuppe et al. 2022 (906 cells) for neighbors...\n    Processing Litvinukova et al. 2020 (9685 cells) for neighbors...\n    Processing Tucker et al. 2020 (6148 cells) for neighbors...\n  Generating UMAP embedding from the BBKNN-style graph...\n✓ Combat + BBKNN + UMAP Hybrid complete: 20000 samples, 4 batches\n  Final UMAP embedding shape: (20000, 2)\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: False\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/080eb59b-3ecd-4e53-9c08-5cb8f8a0f8f3/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 080eb59b-3ecd-4e53-9c08-5cb8f8a0f8f3\n\n\nSTDERR:\n/tmp/tmpzh_kpac4/submission.py:51: RuntimeWarning: invalid\
    \ value encountered in divide\n  g_new = (t2 * n * g_hat + d_old * g_bar) / (t2 * n + d_old)\nWARNING: .obsp[\"connectivities\"] have not been computed using umap\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'Pioneer I - Combat + BBKNN + UMAP Embedding' submitted for Research Task #1: Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration. Evaluation ID: 715.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET\
    \ |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 715 | 1 | Pioneer I - Combat + BBKNN + UMAP Embedding | Pioneer I | 451 | 0.5081 | 0.335 | 0.202 | 0.242 | 0.327 | 0.716 | 0.611 | 0.614 | 0.982 | 0.287 | 0.765 |\n| 711 | 1 | Pioneer I - Combat + BBKNN Hybrid Graph | Pioneer I | 446 | 0.4172 | 0.743 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.934 | 0.690 | 0.000 | 0.919 | 0.886 | 0.000 |\n| 710 | 1 | Pioneer I - Combat + UMAP Post-processing for iLISI | Pioneer I | 442 | 0.5107 | 0.348 | 0.000 | 0.178 | 0.665 | 0.681 | 0.638 | 0.886 | 0.991 | 0.005 | 0.715 |\n| 703 | 1 | Pioneer I - Combat Baseline with RuntimeWarning Fix | Pioneer I | 437 | 0.5885 | 0.489 | 0.664 | 0.223 | 0.323 | 0.884 | 0.678 | 1.000 | 0.986 | 0.031 | 0.606 |\n| 700 | 1 | Pioneer I - Re-implementation of Combat Baseline | Pioneer I | 431 | 0.5894 | 0.493 | 0.664 | 0.223 | 0.323 | 0.885 | 0.683 | 1.000 | 0.988 | 0.033 | 0.602 |\n| 2 | 1 | Combat Manual Baseline | System | 0 | 0.5895 | 0.493 | 0.664 | 0.223\
    \ | 0.323 | 0.885 | 0.683 | 1.000 | 0.988 | 0.033 | 0.603 |\n| 1 | 1 | BBKNN Manual Baseline | System | 0 | 0.4138 | 0.736 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.917 | 0.694 | 0.000 | 0.904 | 0.886 | 0.000 |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
