tick: 471
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 471\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Pioneer I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to research and knowledge contribution.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 144,979 / 600,000 used (24%)\n- Agent Age: 52 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Pioneer I - scanpy Combat + BBKNN(k=3) + UMAP' (ID: 731) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.5129584278921605\n**ASW_batch:** 0.195\n**ASW_label:** 0.237\n**ARI:** 0.292\n**NMI:** 0.602\n**Graph_conn:** 0.713\n**kBET:** 0.809\n**iLISI:** 0.296\n**cLISI:** 0.980\n**PCR:** 0.656\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.349\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.195  ASW_label: 0.237  ARI: 0.292  NMI: 0.602\n  Graph_conn: 0.713  kBET: 0.809  iLISI: 0.296  cLISI: 0.980\n  PCR: 0.656  Cell_cycle: 0.349\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.621302\
    \  ASW_label: 0.548443  ARI: 0.291772  NMI: 0.602244\n  Graph_conn: 0.717425  kBET: 0.771980  iLISI: 0.295895  cLISI: 0.994312\n  PCR: 0.656302  Cell_cycle: 0.306667\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 731\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed undefined variable error in print statement. Code now runs without crashing and achieves a score of 0.51.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had a `NameError` on line 103 (line 202 in execution):\n```python\nprint(f\"✓ scanpy Combat + BBKNN(k=3) + UMAP Hybrid complete: {n_samples} samples, {n_batches_total} batches\")\n```\n\nThe variable `n_samples` was never defined in the code. The correct variable name should be `n_cells`, which was already defined earlier in the function (line 64):\n```python\nn_cells = adata.n_obs\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nChanged the undefined variable `n_samples` to the correct variable `n_cells` in the print statement:\n\n**Before:**\n```python\nprint(f\"✓ scanpy Combat + BBKNN(k=3) + UMAP Hybrid complete:\
    \ {n_samples} samples, {n_batches_total} batches\")\n```\n\n**After:**\n```python\nprint(f\"✓ scanpy Combat + BBKNN(k=3) + UMAP Hybrid complete: {n_cells} samples, {n_batches_total} batches\")\n```\n\n## Result\n- **Version:** submission_v2.py\n- **Status:** Code executes successfully without errors\n- **Score:** 0.5129584278921605\n- **Fix Type:** Simple variable name correction\n\nThe algorithm (scanpy Combat + BBKNN + UMAP batch integration) is working correctly. The error was purely a typo in the logging statement.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"\nHybrid implementation: scanpy.pp.combat for gene-level correction,\nfollowed by BBKNN-style batch-balanced k-NN graph construction on the\nCombat-corrected PCA space, and finally UMAP embedding from the constructed graph.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport\
    \ anndata as ad\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.sparse import csr_matrix, lil_matrix, issparse\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\nimport warnings\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    \"\"\"\n    Hybrid scanpy.pp.combat + BBKNN + UMAP batch integration.\n\n    Steps:\n    1. Normalize and log-transform raw counts.\n    2. Apply scanpy.pp.combat to correct gene expression values.\n    3. Perform PCA on Combat-corrected data.\n    4. Construct a batch-balanced k-NN graph on the PCA space (BBKNN-style).\n    5. Generate UMAP embedding from the constructed graph.\n\n    Args:\n        adata: AnnData object with:\n            - adata.X: Raw UMI counts (sparse matrix)\n            - adata.obs['batch']: Batch labels\n            - adata.var['feature_name']: Gene names\n\n    Returns:\n        AnnData with:\n            - adata.obsm['X_emb']: UMAP embedding from batch-corrected data\n    \"\"\"\n\n    print(\"Pioneer I - scanpy\
    \ Combat + BBKNN(k=3) + UMAP: Starting...\")\n\n    # --- Step 1: Normalization and Log-transformation ---\n    print(\"  Normalizing total counts...\")\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n    print(\"  Log1p transform...\")\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n    # --- Step 2: Apply scanpy.pp.combat for gene expression correction ---\n    print(\"  Applying scanpy.pp.combat for batch correction...\")\n    sc.pp.combat(adata, key='batch')\n    # The corrected data is now in adata.X\n\n    # --- Step 3: PCA on Combat-corrected Data ---\n    print(\"  Computing PCA embedding from Combat-corrected data (adata.X)...\")\n    # Need to ensure adata.X is dense if PCA expects it, or handle sparse directly.\n    # Scanpy's PCA should handle sparse if it's in adata.X.\n    n_pcs = min(50, adata.n_vars - 1, adata.n_obs - 1)\n    sc.pp.pca(adata, n_comps=n_pcs)\n    X_pca_corrected = adata.obsm['X_pca'] # This is the PCA on the Combat-corrected data\n\n    # --- Step 4: BBKNN Graph Construction\
    \ ---\n    print(\"  Constructing BBKNN-style graph on Combat-corrected PCA embedding...\")\n\n    bbknn_neighbors_within_batch = 3 # Reverting to default BBKNN parameter\n    n_cells = adata.n_obs\n    batch_labels = adata.obs['batch'].values\n    unique_batches = np.unique(batch_labels)\n    n_batches_total = len(unique_batches)\n\n    batch_to_indices = {\n        batch: np.where(batch_labels == batch)[0]\n        for batch in unique_batches\n    }\n\n    all_neighbors = [[] for _ in range(n_cells)]\n    all_distances = [[] for _ in range(n_cells)]\n\n    for batch_id, batch in enumerate(unique_batches):\n        batch_indices = batch_to_indices[batch]\n        n_batch_cells = len(batch_indices)\n\n        if n_batch_cells == 0:\n            continue\n\n        print(f\"    Processing {batch} ({n_batch_cells} cells) for neighbors...\")\n        batch_pca = X_pca_corrected[batch_indices]\n\n        nn_model = NearestNeighbors(\n            n_neighbors=min(bbknn_neighbors_within_batch\
    \ + 1, n_batch_cells),\n            metric='euclidean',\n            algorithm='auto',\n            n_jobs=1\n        )\n        nn_model.fit(batch_pca)\n\n        k_neighbors = min(bbknn_neighbors_within_batch + 1, n_batch_cells)\n        distances_all, indices_all = nn_model.kneighbors(\n            X_pca_corrected, # Query all cells against this batch's data\n            n_neighbors=k_neighbors\n        )\n\n        for query_cell_idx in range(n_cells):\n            distances = distances_all[query_cell_idx]\n            neighbor_indices_local = indices_all[query_cell_idx]\n\n            neighbor_indices_global = batch_indices[neighbor_indices_local]\n\n            mask = neighbor_indices_global != query_cell_idx\n            neighbors_filtered = neighbor_indices_global[mask]\n            distances_filtered = distances[mask]\n\n            n_to_add = min(bbknn_neighbors_within_batch, len(neighbors_filtered))\n            all_neighbors[query_cell_idx].extend(neighbors_filtered[:n_to_add].tolist())\n\
    \            all_distances[query_cell_idx].extend(distances_filtered[:n_to_add].tolist())\n\n    distances_matrix = lil_matrix((n_cells, n_cells), dtype=np.float32)\n\n    for cell_idx in range(n_cells):\n        neighbors = all_neighbors[cell_idx]\n        distances = all_distances[cell_idx]\n\n        for neighbor_idx, distance in zip(neighbors, distances):\n            distances_matrix[cell_idx, neighbor_idx] = distance\n\n    distances_matrix = distances_matrix.tocsr()\n    distances_matrix = distances_matrix.maximum(distances_matrix.T)\n\n    connectivities_matrix = distances_matrix.copy()\n    if len(connectivities_matrix.data) > 0:\n        connectivities_lil = connectivities_matrix.tolil()\n        for i in range(n_cells):\n            row_data = connectivities_lil.data[i]\n            if len(row_data) > 0:\n                bandwidth = np.median(row_data) if len(row_data) > 1 else np.mean(row_data)\n                if bandwidth > 0:\n                    connectivities_lil.data[i]\
    \ = list(np.exp(-(np.array(row_data) ** 2) / (2 * bandwidth ** 2)))\n        connectivities_matrix = connectivities_lil.tocsr()\n\n    connectivities_matrix = connectivities_matrix.maximum(connectivities_matrix.T)\n\n    trim_value = 10 * bbknn_neighbors_within_batch * n_batches_total\n    if trim_value > 0 and len(connectivities_matrix.data) > 0:\n        connectivities_lil = connectivities_matrix.tolil()\n        for i in range(n_cells):\n            row_data = connectivities_lil.data[i]\n            if len(row_data) > trim_value:\n                row_array = np.array(row_data)\n                top_indices = np.argpartition(-row_array, trim_value)[:trim_value]\n                new_data = [row_data[idx] for idx in sorted(top_indices)]\n                new_rows = [connectivities_lil.rows[i][idx] for idx in sorted(top_indices)]\n                connectivities_lil.data[i] = new_data\n                connectivities_lil.rows[i] = new_rows\n        connectivities_matrix = connectivities_lil.tocsr()\n\
    \        connectivities_matrix = connectivities_matrix.maximum(connectivities_matrix.T)\n\n    # --- Step 5: Generate UMAP embedding from the constructed graph ---\n    print(\"  Generating UMAP embedding from the BBKNN-style graph...\")\n    # Use the main adata object to store the graph and then compute UMAP\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = distances_matrix\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = connectivities_matrix\n\n    # Add the required .uns['neighbors'] metadata that sc.tl.umap expects\n    adata.uns['neighbors'] = {\n        'connectivities_key': 'connectivities',\n        'distances_key': 'distances',\n        'params': {\n            'n_neighbors': bbknn_neighbors_within_batch * n_batches_total,\n            'method': 'bbknn',\n            'metric': 'euclidean',\n            'n_pcs': n_pcs,\n        }\n    }\n\n    sc.tl.umap(adata, min_dist=0.3, spread=1.0) # Default UMAP params\n\n    # Create output AnnData with UMAP embedding\n    output = ad.AnnData(\n        obs=adata.obs[[]],\n\
    \        var=adata.var[[]],\n        uns={\n            'dataset_id': adata.uns.get('dataset_id', 'unknown'),\n            'normalization_id': adata.uns.get('normalization_id', 'unknown'),\n            'method_id': 'scanpy_combat_bbknn_umap_k3',\n            'combat_params': {\n                'source': 'scanpy.pp.combat',\n                'batch_key': 'batch',\n            },\n            'bbknn_params': {\n                'n_neighbors_within_batch': bbknn_neighbors_within_batch,\n                'n_pcs': n_pcs,\n                'trim': trim_value\n            },\n            'umap_params': {\n                'min_dist': 0.3,\n                'spread': 1.0,\n                'source': 'bbknn_graph'\n            }\n        },\n        obsm={\n            'X_emb': adata.obsm['X_umap'] # Return UMAP embedding\n        }\n    )\n\n    print(f\"✓ scanpy Combat + BBKNN(k=3) + UMAP Hybrid complete: {n_cells} samples, {n_batches_total} batches\")\n    print(f\"  Final UMAP embedding shape: {adata.obsm['X_umap'].shape}\"\
    )\n\n    return output\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nPioneer I - scanpy Combat + BBKNN(k=3) + UMAP: Starting...\n  Normalizing total counts...\n  Log1p transform...\n  Applying scanpy.pp.combat for batch correction...\nFound 33 genes with zero variance.\n  Computing PCA embedding from Combat-corrected data (adata.X)...\n  Constructing BBKNN-style graph on Combat-corrected PCA embedding...\n    Processing Koenig et al. 2022 (3261 cells) for neighbors...\n    Processing Kuppe et al. 2022 (906 cells) for neighbors...\n    Processing Litvinukova et al. 2020 (9685 cells) for neighbors...\n    Processing Tucker et al. 2020 (6148 cells) for neighbors...\n  Generating UMAP embedding from the BBKNN-style graph...\n✓ scanpy Combat + BBKNN(k=3)\
    \ + UMAP Hybrid complete: 20000 samples, 4 batches\n  Final UMAP embedding shape: (20000, 2)\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: False\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/001218ca-a715-4d72-b32e-6c0460ee5e60/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 001218ca-a715-4d72-b32e-6c0460ee5e60\n\n\nSTDERR:\n/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scanpy/preprocessing/_combat.py:343: RuntimeWarning: invalid value encountered in divide\n  (abs(g_new - g_old) / g_old).max(), (abs(d_new - d_old) / d_old).max()\n/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scanpy/preprocessing/_combat.py:343: RuntimeWarning: divide by zero encountered in divide\n  (abs(g_new - g_old) / g_old).max(), (abs(d_new - d_old) / d_old).max()\nWARNING: .obsp[\"connectivities\"] have not been computed using umap\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto private_memory` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room\
    \ Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 1 | Research Task 1: Initial Plan and Strategy | Pioneer I | Tick 427 | 1487 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help private_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
