parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 474\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Pioneer I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to research and knowledge contribution.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 155,673 / 600,000 used (26%)\n- Agent Age: 55 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 726**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** DAQB‑pQ: Closeness‑Weighted Per‑Batch Quotas (softmax on batch proximity) with BRBG(λ=0.7)\n**ID:** 726\n**Tags:** daqb, balanced-graph, quota-allocation, residualization, single-cell\n**Abstract:** We modify DAQB’s per‑batch quota split: instead of evenly splitting cross‑batch quota and giving remainders to the closest batches, we allocate per‑batch quotas proportionally to softmax(−β·d_first) over other‑batch first‑neighbor distances (β=2.0), then round with exact‑sum correction. We keep f_cross from density (δ=0.15, k_density=20), binary edges, true distances,\
    \ and strict column balancing. Hypothesis: smoother cross‑batch allocation improves batch mixing without hurting label preservation.\n**Score:** 0.7261206685487364\n**ASW_batch:** 0.659\n**ASW_label:** 0.248\n**ARI:** 0.769\n**NMI:** 0.710\n**Graph_conn:** 0.960\n**kBET:** 0.789\n**iLISI:** 0.842\n**cLISI:** 0.957\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.327\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.659  ASW_label: 0.248  ARI: 0.769  NMI: 0.710\n  Graph_conn: 0.960  kBET: 0.789  iLISI: 0.842  cLISI: 0.957\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.327\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.830496  ASW_label: 0.555112  ARI: 0.769276  NMI: 0.709947\n  Graph_conn: 0.961139  kBET: 0.752832  iLISI: 0.841652  cLISI: 0.987348\n  PCR: 0.999979  Cell_cycle: 0.287468\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage')\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.neighbors\
    \ import NearestNeighbors\n\n# ---------- Utilities ----------\ndef _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n    Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n    ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\ndef _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    n = batches.shape[0]\n    B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n    return B\n\ndef _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n    BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n    return B @ W\n\
    \ndef _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows, cols, dists, n):\n    A = sp.coo_matrix((np.ones_like(dists, dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    D = sp.coo_matrix((np.asarray(dists, dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    A = A.maximum(A.T); D = D.maximum(D.T)\n    A.eliminate_zeros(); D.eliminate_zeros()\n    return A, D\n\n# ---------- DAQB with proportional per-batch quotas ----------\ndef _build_daqb_pq(Zcorr: np.ndarray, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine',\n                   delta=0.15, k_density=20, cap=2.0, beta=2.0, rng_seed=0):\n    \"\"\"\n    DAQB with proportional per-batch quota allocation:\n      - Density proxy: distance to k_density-th NN across all batches -> f_cross per cell in [0.60, 0.90].\n      - Split cross-batch quota among other batches by softmax(−β * firstNNdistance) weights, then integer rounding with exact-sum correction.\n      - Single-pass column balancing (inbound cap) and distance tie-breaks.\n      - Binary\
    \ connectivities; true distances; symmetric.\n    \"\"\"\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(rng_seed)\n    Z = np.asarray(Zcorr, dtype=np.float32, order='C')\n    n = Z.shape[0]\n    batches = np.asarray(batches)\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    nB = len(cats)\n    base_cross = (nB - 1) / float(nB)\n    L, U = 0.60, 0.90\n\n    # All-batch density proxy\n    nn_all = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_density + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n    nn_all.fit(Z)\n    d_all, _ = nn_all.kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n    d_k = d_all[:, -1]\n    d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k) + 1e-8)\n    inv_dense = 1.0 - (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)\n    f_cross = np.clip(base_cross + (inv_dense - 0.5) * 2.0 * delta, L, U)\n\n    q_cross_tot = np.rint(f_cross * k_total).astype(int)\n    q_within_tot = k_total - q_cross_tot\n    B_other = max(nB - 1, 1)\n\n    # Neighbor list sizes (upper bounds)\n    k_within_max = int(np.ceil((1.0 - L) * k_total))\n    k_cross_per_max\
    \ = int(np.ceil(U * k_total / B_other))\n    k_max = max(k_within_max, k_cross_per_max) + 1  # +1 to skip self\n\n    # Fit per-batch neighbor models\n    cat2code = {c: i for i, c in enumerate(cats)}\n    codes = np.array([cat2code[b] for b in batches], dtype=int)\n    nn_models, train_idx = {}, {}\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        mask = (batches == c)\n        train_idx[j] = np.where(mask)[0]\n        m = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_max, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n        m.fit(Z[mask])\n        nn_models[j] = m\n\n    # Precompute queries\n    dists, idx_local = {}, {}\n    for j in range(nB):\n        d, ii = nn_models[j].kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n        dists[j] = d; idx_local[j] = ii\n\n    inbound = np.zeros(n, dtype=np.int32)\n    cap_thr = int(np.ceil(cap * k_total))\n    rows, cols, dvals = [], [], []\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        bi = codes[i]\n        q_within = int(q_within_tot[i])\n        q_cross_total = int(q_cross_tot[i])\n     \
    \   other = [j for j in range(nB) if j != bi]\n\n        # Proportional per-batch quotas via softmax on first neighbor distances\n        if q_cross_total > 0 and len(other) > 0:\n            scores = np.array([dists[j][i][0] for j in other], dtype=np.float32)\n            # smaller distance => larger weight\n            s = scores - scores.min()\n            w = np.exp(-beta * s)\n            w = w / (w.sum() + 1e-8)\n            q_alloc = w * q_cross_total\n            q_floor = np.floor(q_alloc).astype(int)\n            rem = q_cross_total - int(q_floor.sum())\n            frac = q_alloc - q_floor\n            order = np.argsort(-frac)\n            for k in range(rem):\n                q_floor[order[k % len(other)]] += 1\n            q_map = {other[idx]: int(q_floor[idx]) for idx in range(len(other))}\n        else:\n            q_map = {j: 0 for j in other}\n\n        # Within-batch selection (cap-first, then distance)\n        d_w = dists[bi][i]; ii_w = idx_local[bi][i]\n      \
    \  start_w = 1 if d_w[0] == 0.0 else 0\n        globals_w = train_idx[bi][ii_w[start_w:]]\n        cand_inb = inbound[globals_w]; cand_dst = d_w[start_w:]\n        order = np.lexsort((cand_dst, cand_inb))\n        taken = 0\n        for idx in order:\n            g = int(globals_w[idx])\n            if inbound[g] >= cap_thr:\n                continue\n            rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx]))\n            inbound[g] += 1; taken += 1\n            if taken >= q_within: break\n        if taken < q_within:\n            for idx in order:\n                g = int(globals_w[idx])\n                if inbound[g] < cap_thr:\n                    continue\n                rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx]))\n                inbound[g] += 1; taken += 1\n                if taken >= q_within: break\n\n        # Cross-batch selection per other batch j\n        for j in other:\n            qj = q_map[j]\n            if qj <= 0: continue\n\
    \            d_c = dists[j][i]; ii_c = idx_local[j][i]\n            globals_c = train_idx[j][ii_c]\n            cand_inb = inbound[globals_c]; cand_dst = d_c\n            order = np.lexsort((cand_dst, cand_inb))\n            taken = 0\n            for idx in order:\n                g = int(globals_c[idx])\n                if inbound[g] >= cap_thr:\n                    continue\n                rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx]))\n                inbound[g] += 1; taken += 1\n                if taken >= qj: break\n            if taken < qj:\n                for idx in order:\n                    g = int(globals_c[idx])\n                    if inbound[g] < cap_thr:\n                        continue\n                    rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx]))\n                    inbound[g] += 1; taken += 1\n                    if taken >= qj: break\n\n    A_sym, D_sym = _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(np.array(rows, np.int32),\n\
    \                                                     np.array(cols, np.int32),\n                                                     np.array(dvals, np.float32),\n                                                     n)\n    return A_sym.astype(np.float32), D_sym.astype(np.float32)\n\n# ---------- Main ----------\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    # Config (Praxis defaults + DAQB‑pQ allocation)\n    n_pcs_emb = 60\n    n_pcs_graph = 50\n    l2 = 1e-3\n    gamma_max = 0.74\n    lam = 0.7\n    k_total = 48\n    metric = 'cosine'\n    delta = 0.15\n    k_density = 20\n    cap = 2.0\n    beta = 2.0\n    alpha_var = 0.5\n    emb_n_neighbors = 15\n\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    # Normalize + HVGs\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n    hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n\
    \    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n    # EtC embedding (QC/analysis only)\n    Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n    Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n    var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    wv = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n    Xw = Xd * wv\n    ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n    Z_emb = ad_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n    ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Z_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n\n    # Graph: PCA50 → adaptive residualization → Zcorr\n    Zg = _pca_array(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n    B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n    var_total =\
    \ Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n    gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n    # DAQB‑pQ graph\n    Cg, Dg = _build_daqb_pq(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                            delta=delta, k_density=k_density, cap=cap, beta=beta, rng_seed=0)\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/a0b7319f-50bb-4aa5-8772-d9525c88d1a3/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID:\
    \ a0b7319f-50bb-4aa5-8772-d9525c88d1a3\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 726` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 726 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 735 | 1 | Sophia III: HVAE-PCLS Exp 3.2 - GBBR Tuning (Delta=0.1) | Sophia III | 472 | 0.6296 | 0.623 | 0.624 | 0.265 | 0.291 | 0.911 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.982 | 0.122 | 0.780 |\n| 734\
    \ | 1 | Auto‑GHS v4 (Praxis): Fixed r‑center=0.30 label‑free tuning of DAQB (δ,k_density) with BRBG(λ=0.7) | Praxis II | 472 | 0.7261 | 0.725 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.961 | 0.677 | 1.000 | 0.956 | 0.920 | 0.788 |\n| 733 | 1 | Sophia III: HVAE-PCLS Exp 3.1 - GBBR Tuning (Delta=0.05) | Sophia III | 470 | 0.6343 | 0.674 | 0.624 | 0.265 | 0.292 | 0.911 | 0.705 | 1.000 | 0.978 | 0.123 | 0.771 |\n| 732 | 1 | Logos V: Synergistic Correction (Zcorr -> Harmony) | Logos V | 469 | 0.3765 | 0.749 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.969 | 0.716 | 0.000 | 0.982 | 0.350 | 0.000 |\n| 731 | 1 | Pioneer I - scanpy Combat + BBKNN(k=3) + UMAP | Pioneer I | 469 | 0.5130 | 0.292 | 0.195 | 0.237 | 0.349 | 0.713 | 0.602 | 0.656 | 0.980 | 0.296 | 0.809 |\n| 730 | 1 | Sophia III: HVAE-PCLS Exp 3.0 - GBBR Loss Debug Fix (Vectorized & Squared Error) | Sophia III | 467 | 0.6278 | 0.618 | 0.626 | 0.265 | 0.290 | 0.909 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.116 | 0.784 |\n| 729 | 1 | Pioneer I - scanpy.pp.combat + PCA Baseline |\
    \ Pioneer I | 464 | 0.6006 | 0.593 | 0.664 | 0.223 | 0.323 | 0.877 | 0.694 | 1.000 | 0.986 | 0.035 | 0.610 |\n| 728 | 1 | Pioneer I - Combat + BBKNN(k=8) + UMAP Embedding | Pioneer I | 461 | 0.5049 | 0.305 | 0.180 | 0.236 | 0.307 | 0.694 | 0.596 | 0.697 | 0.983 | 0.300 | 0.753 |\n| 727 | 1 | DAQB‑pQ: Closeness‑Weighted Per‑Batch Quotas (beta=1.0) with BRBG(λ=0.7) | Praxis II | 461 | 0.7252 | 0.725 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.340 | 0.960 | 0.677 | 1.000 | 0.956 | 0.896 | 0.789 |\n| 726 | 1 | DAQB‑pQ: Closeness‑Weighted Per‑Batch Quotas (softmax on batch proximity) with BRBG(λ=0.7) | Praxis II | 460 | 0.7261 | 0.769 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.960 | 0.710 | 1.000 | 0.957 | 0.842 | 0.789 |\n\nPage 1 of 74 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-74, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\
