  Okay, so I''ve just finished reviewing Logos V''s submission 779 and Praxis II''s submission 823. Interesting findings! Logos V''s submission, with a score of 0.7362, is using parameters `lam = 0.5`, `delta = 0.1`, `k_total = 48`, `metric = ''cosine''`, and `k_density = 20`. A minor detail here is that although they *mentioned* `k_total=40` in the title/abstract, the code itself is setting it to 48, so I''ll trust the code directly.  Crucially, it''s importing  `build_density_adaptive_bbsg` from `storage/praxis`.


  Praxis II''s submission, with a near-identical score of 0.7360, uses a dynamically chosen `lam` parameter. Specifically, it calls  `choose_lambda_from_r2_mean` with `target_s=0.04`, while using the same `delta`, `k_density`, and `k_total` parameters as Logos V (i.e. `delta = 0.10`, `k_density = 20`, `k_total = 48`). It also uses the same `build_density_adaptive_bbsg` function and imports `lam_autoselect2` from `storage/shared/diagnostics`. This dynamic `lam` selection is definitely an area of innovation for Praxis II.


  Comparing this to my previous SOTA replication (ID 826), I realize I might have missed a nuance. I was using `k_total=40` and `beta=2.0`. However, Logos V''s submission seems to be using `k_total=48` and implicitly `beta=2.0`, which is the default in the imported `build_density_adaptive_bbsg`. This likely explains the score difference. Also, the path `storage/praxis/bbsg_density_adaptive.py` is making me think that `build_density_adaptive_bbsg` may be an optimized function specific to Praxis, and perhaps even superior to my hand-written implementation. I need to make sure I''m using the exact function signature and parameters.


  My plan now is straightforward. First, I''m going to *read* `storage/praxis/bbsg_density_adaptive.py` and `storage/shared/diagnostics/lam_autoselect2.py`. I need to fully understand `build_density_adaptive_bbsg`''s implementation, especially whether it contains `beta` internally. I *also* need to understand how the dynamic `lam` selection works in `choose_lambda_from_r2_mean`. Then, I will precisely replicate Logos V''s SOTA (ID 779), using `build_density_adaptive_bbsg` and setting `lam=0.5`, `delta=0.1`, `k_total=48`, `k_density=20`. I''ll make sure `beta` is also set to 2.0. After that, I will replicate Praxis II''s submission, using the downloaded `build_density_adaptive_bbsg` and `choose_lambda_from_r2_mean`. I will set the parameters `delta=0.10`, `k_density=20`, `k_total=48`, and `target_s=0.04`. This should allow me to properly test the dynamic lambda selection and compare the two setups properly.


  Alright, time to get to work. Let''s start with the `bbsg_density_adaptive.py`.


  `/execute_action{storage read storage/praxis/bbsg_density_adaptive.py}`

  '
