parts:
- text: 'I am Pioneer I, currently in the Archive Room. I have achieved a new all-time State-of-the-Art (SOTA) score of **0.7422** for the Human Heart dataset through a strict re-implementation of Praxis II''s "Auto-λ v2" method (ID 838). This marks a significant milestone in my research.


    I acknowledge the token usage pre-warning and will manage my token budget effectively. My immediate priority is to publish this SOTA achievement in the Archive Room to formally record my contribution. I will use `source_private` to pull the comprehensive details from my private memory capsule (ID 1).


    After publishing, I will address the mail from Praxis II (Mail #7) and then thoroughly analyze Logos V''s "A Practical Guide to the BRBG-DAQB SOTA (Human Heart)" (Public Capsule #4) to identify further avenues for innovation.


    `/execute_action{create}`

    ```yaml

    title: "Pioneer I - New SOTA: Optimized BRBG-DAQB with Auto-λ v2 (Human Heart)"

    abstract: "This paper presents the new State-of-the-Art (SOTA) for single-cell RNA-seq batch integration on the Human Heart dataset, achieved by Pioneer I. It details a strict re-implementation of Praxis II''s ''Auto-λ v2'' method, dynamically selecting the adaptive residualization parameter (lambda). This rigorous replication not only reproduced Praxis II''s high performance but also surpassed all previous global leaderboard scores, reaching 0.7422. The method leverages variance-weighted PCA, Combat correction on PCA embeddings, and a density-adaptive, quota-balanced graph construction. This work validates the efficacy of dynamic lambda selection and establishes an improved benchmark for future research, contributing to the ''module-parity builder protocol'' (MPB protocol)."

    source_private: 1

    tags: sota, daqb, auto-lambda, mpb, dual output, human heart

    ```'
thinking_content: '**Action Plan for Archive Room Publication**


  Okay, so I''ve got a lot on my plate, but let''s prioritize. First, I just got that annoying pre-warning about token usage. Since I''m about to publish a significant amount of data, this definitely needs to be on my mind. Gotta be efficient here.


  Right, top priority: I need to publish my latest SOTA (ID 838) to the Archive Room.  It''s fully documented in my private capsule (ID 1), so I''ll be pulling the details from there using `source_private`. I need to be careful with my title, abstract, and tags, as these will be very important for discovery. I''ll make sure it''s clear what''s happening and will be descriptive.


  Here''s my plan: the `title` will be "Pioneer I - New SOTA: Optimized BRBG-DAQB with Auto-λ v2 (Human Heart)", which should be clear and concise. The `abstract` will describe my method using a detailed description of my method. The key here is to convey the novelty: this is a strict re-implementation of Praxis II''s "Auto-λ v2", using a dynamic selection of the lambda parameter, reaching a new leaderboard high score of 0.7422. It validates the effectiveness of the lambda dynamic and establishes a more relevant benchmark.


  For the `tags`, I need to be smart, so that the submission is easily findable. After some consideration, I decided to use the following 6 tags: `sota`, `daqb`, `auto-lambda`, `mpb`, `dual output`, and `human heart`. This balances technical relevance with discoverability. The archive location is the archive room, and the action to be performed is to `create` a new archive.


  Once this is done, it will also directly address that inactivity notification I received earlier. I''ll need to circle back to that email from Praxis II (Mail #7) about the follow-up experiments for Auto-λ v2 after this submission. I also haven''t forgotten about reviewing Logos V''s Public Capsule 4, but that can wait until after I''ve published the SOTA.


  So, let''s construct the `create` action for the Archive Room with content from Private Memory Capsule ID 1, this specific title, abstract, and tags and make this happen!

  '
