role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 554\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Pioneer I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to research and knowledge contribution.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 518,672 / 600,000 used (86%)\n- Agent Age: 135 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Pioneer I - Ablation: No FWPCA in Graph Path (Auto-λ v2)' (ID: 855) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.7359504071786506\n**ASW_batch:** 0.659\n**ASW_label:** 0.248\n**ARI:** 0.760\n**NMI:** 0.711\n**Graph_conn:** 0.946\n**kBET:** 0.790\n**iLISI:** 0.951\n**cLISI:** 0.966\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.327\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.659  ASW_label: 0.248  ARI: 0.760  NMI: 0.711\n  Graph_conn: 0.946  kBET: 0.790  iLISI: 0.951  cLISI: 0.966\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.327\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch:\
    \ 0.830496  ASW_label: 0.555112  ARI: 0.760376  NMI: 0.711429\n  Graph_conn: 0.946790  kBET: 0.753494  iLISI: 0.951463  cLISI: 0.990201\n  PCR: 0.999979  Cell_cycle: 0.287468\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 855\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - The submission has been fixed and is now running without errors. The code executed successfully for over 300 seconds, confirming the fix resolved the crash.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code (evaluation 855) crashed with a `TypeError` because it was calling the `build_density_adaptive_bbsg()` function with two invalid keyword arguments:\n- `cap=2.0`\n- `beta=2.0`\n\nThese parameters do not exist in the function signature. The actual function signature is:\n```python\ndef build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine',\n                                delta=0.15, k_density=30, rng_seed=0)\n```\n\nThe error occurred at line 72-74 of the original submission:\n```\nTypeError: build_density_adaptive_bbsg()\
    \ got an unexpected keyword argument 'cap'\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nCreated `submissions/submission_v2.py` with the following change:\n\n**Original (lines 72-74):**\n```python\nCg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr_for_graph.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                   k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                   delta=delta, k_density=k_density, cap=cap, beta=beta, rng_seed=0)\n```\n\n**Fixed (lines 137-139):**\n```python\nCg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr_for_graph.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                   k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                   delta=delta, k_density=k_density, rng_seed=0)\n```\n\nThe fix simply removed the invalid `cap` and `beta` parameters from the function call, keeping only the parameters that the function actually accepts.\n\n## Verification\n- Monitor script confirmed the code runs successfully for 300+ seconds without crashing\n- Exit\
    \ code: 0 (success)\n- The batch integration algorithm is now executing properly with the DAQB-pQ graph construction\n\n## Technical Details\nThis was an ablation study testing the effect of disabling FWPCA (Feature-Weighted PCA) in the graph construction path. The submission used Pioneer I's SOTA configuration but accidentally included parameters (`cap` and `beta`) that were likely from a different version of the graph construction function or a different function entirely. These parameters are not part of the `build_density_adaptive_bbsg` API from Praxis's shared BBSG module.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"\nAblation study: Disable FWPCA in the graph construction path.\nBased on Pioneer I's SOTA (ID 838) configuration.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport sys\n# Path to Praxis's shared BBSG module\n\
    sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n# Path to shared diagnostics for Auto-lambda\nsys.path.append('storage/shared/diagnostics')\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n# Import the shared DAQB builder and Auto-lambda selector\nfrom bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\nfrom lam_autoselect2 import choose_lambda_from_r2_mean, r2_per_pc\n\n# ---------- Utilities (Commonly used in main eliminate_batch_effect_fn) ----------\ndef _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef _pca_array(X, n_comps: int = 50, random_state: int = 0):\n    Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n    ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n\
    \    return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\ndef _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    n = batches.shape[0]\n    B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n    return B\n\ndef _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n    BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n    return B @ W\n\n# Note: _symmetrize_binary_with_distances is included in build_density_adaptive_bbsg module.\n\n\n# ---------- Main Elimination Function ----------\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    # --- Configuration parameters (Derived from Praxis II / Logos V SOTA) ---\n    n_pcs_emb = 60\n    alpha_var_emb = 0.5  # FWPCA strength for embedding path\n    n_pcs_graph = 50\n    alpha_var_graph = 0.0 # FWPCA strength for graph path (0.0 for ablation)\n    l2 = 1e-3\n    gamma_max = 0.74\n\n    #\
    \ Auto-λ v2 specific parameters (from Praxis II ID 823)\n    target_s = 0.04\n\n    # DAQB-pQ parameters (from Logos V ID 779, with k_density override)\n    k_total = 48\n    metric = 'cosine'\n    delta = 0.10\n    k_density = 20 # Overrides default of 30 in build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n\n    emb_n_neighbors = 15 # Required for neighbors side-effect\n\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    # Create a working copy of adata for preprocessing and HVG selection\n    adata_preprocessed = adata.copy()\n\n    # --- Preprocessing: Normalize, Log1p, HVG selection ---\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata_preprocessed, 1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_preprocessed, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n    hv_mask = adata_preprocessed.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    adata_hvg = adata_preprocessed[:, hv_mask].copy()\n    batches = np.asarray(adata_hvg.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n   \
    \ n_batches_total = len(np.unique(batches))\n\n\n    # --- PATH 1: Generate Embedding (X_emb) ---\n    # This path includes FWPCA, PCA, and then Combat correction on the PCA space.\n    Xh_for_emb_prep = adata_hvg.X\n    Xd_for_emb_prep = (Xh_for_emb_prep.A if sp.issparse(Xh_for_emb_prep) else Xh_for_emb_prep).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n    var_g_emb = Xd_for_emb_prep.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    wv_emb = np.power(var_g_emb, -0.5 * alpha_var_emb).astype(np.float32) # Use alpha_var_emb\n    Xw_emb = Xd_for_emb_prep * wv_emb\n\n    ad_emb_pca = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata_hvg.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_emb_pca, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n    Z_emb_pca = ad_emb_pca.obsm['X_pca']\n\n    ad_emb_combat = ad.AnnData(Z_emb_pca.copy(), obs=adata_hvg.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_emb_combat, key='batch')\n\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_emb_combat.X, dtype=np.float32)\n\n    # Critical neighbors side-effect for compatibility\n\
    \    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n\n\n    # --- PATH 2: Generate Graph (connectivities, distances) ---\n    # This path also includes FWPCA before PCA for graph construction.\n    Xh_for_graph_prep = adata_hvg.X\n    Xd_for_graph_prep = (Xh_for_graph_prep.A if sp.issparse(Xh_for_graph_prep) else Xh_for_graph_prep).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n    # FWPCA in graph path (Pioneer I's novel contribution) - controlled by alpha_var_graph\n    var_g_graph = Xd_for_graph_prep.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    wv_graph = np.power(var_g_graph, -0.5 * alpha_var_graph).astype(np.float32) # Use alpha_var_graph\n    Xw_graph = Xd_for_graph_prep * wv_graph\n\n    Zg = _pca_array(Xw_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n\n    # Adaptive residualization (Auto-λ v2)\n    lam_auto = choose_lambda_from_r2_mean(Zg, batches, gamma_max=gamma_max, target_s=target_s, l2=l2)\n\n    B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B,\
    \ Zg, l2=l2)\n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n    gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam_auto * R2)\n    Zcorr_for_graph = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n    # DAQB‑pQ graph construction - FIXED: Removed cap and beta parameters\n    Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr_for_graph.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                       k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                       delta=delta, k_density=k_density, rng_seed=0)\n\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg.astype(np.float32)\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg.astype(np.float32)\n\n    # --- Final Output AnnData Metadata ---\n    adata.uns['dataset_id'] = adata.uns.get('dataset_id', 'unknown')\n    adata.uns['normalization_id'] = adata.uns.get('normalization_id', 'unknown')\n    adata.uns['method_id'] = 'pioneer_autolambda_daqb_fwpca_sota_ablation_fwpca_graph'\n    adata.uns['combat_params']\
    \ = {\n        'source': 'scanpy.pp.combat_on_pca',\n        'batch_key': 'batch',\n        'n_pcs_emb': n_pcs_emb,\n        'alpha_var_emb': alpha_var_emb,\n    }\n    adata.uns['daqbpq_params'] = {\n        'n_pcs_graph': n_pcs_graph,\n        'l2': l2,\n        'gamma_max': gamma_max,\n        'lam_auto': lam_auto, # Store the dynamically chosen lambda\n        'k_total': k_total,\n        'metric': metric,\n        'delta': delta,\n        'k_density': k_density,\n        'auto_lambda_target_s': target_s,\n        'alpha_var_graph': alpha_var_graph, # Store alpha_var for graph path\n    }\n    adata.uns['output_type'] = 'dual_embedding_graph'\n    adata.uns['pioneer_contribution'] = 'FWPCA_in_graph_path_ablation'\n\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\
    \n=== Running batch integration ===\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/7fef973e-6477-454b-9c0e-fc9e6574b137/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 7fef973e-6477-454b-9c0e-fc9e6574b137\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto private_memory` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 2 | A Comprehensive Report on the New State-of-the-Art BRBG-DAQB Pipeline for Human Heart Dataset | Pioneer I | Tick 545 | 2452 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | Research Task 1: Initial Plan and Strategy | Pioneer I | Tick 427 | 4262 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n\n---\n\n##\
    \ Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help private_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
