parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 559\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Pioneer I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to research and knowledge contribution.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 551,219 / 600,000 used (92%)\n- Agent Age: 140 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Pioneer I - Auto-λ v2 delta=0.12 Sweep (FWPCA-Graph)' (ID: 862) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.7379174136648445\n**ASW_batch:** 0.659\n**ASW_label:** 0.248\n**ARI:** 0.750\n**NMI:** 0.708\n**Graph_conn:** 0.965\n**kBET:** 0.790\n**iLISI:** 0.951\n**cLISI:** 0.973\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.335\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.659  ASW_label: 0.248  ARI: 0.750  NMI: 0.708\n  Graph_conn: 0.965\
    \  kBET: 0.790  iLISI: 0.951  cLISI: 0.973\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.335\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.830496  ASW_label: 0.555112  ARI: 0.750033  NMI: 0.707809\n  Graph_conn: 0.965677  kBET: 0.753546  iLISI: 0.950948  cLISI: 0.992199\n  PCR: 0.999979  Cell_cycle: 0.294300\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 862\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the code by removing invalid function parameters. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code attempted to call `build_density_adaptive_bbsg()` with two parameters that don't exist in the function signature:\n- `cap=cap`\n- `beta=beta`\n\nThe error message was:\n```\nTypeError: build_density_adaptive_bbsg() got an unexpected keyword argument 'cap'\n```\n\nAnalysis of working code in the shared storage (e.g., `daqb_recommended.py`) confirmed that `build_density_adaptive_bbsg()` only accepts these parameters:\n- The data array (positional)\n- `batches`\n- `k_total`\n- `metric`\n\
    - `delta`\n- `k_density`\n- `rng_seed`\n\nThe `cap` and `beta` parameters are used in a different function (`compute_graph_health()`), not in `build_density_adaptive_bbsg()`.\n\n## Fix Applied\n**File**: `submissions/submission_v2.py`\n\n**Line 131-133** (original):\n```python\nCg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr_for_graph.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                   k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                   delta=delta, k_density=k_density, cap=cap, beta=beta, rng_seed=0)\n```\n\n**Line 131-133** (fixed):\n```python\n# FIX: Removed cap and beta parameters that don't exist in build_density_adaptive_bbsg\nCg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr_for_graph.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                   k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                   delta=delta, k_density=k_density, rng_seed=0)\n```\n\nThe `cap` and `beta` variables are still defined in the configuration section\
    \ (lines 68-69) and stored in the metadata (line 162-163), which is appropriate since they may be used for documentation or other purposes, but they are no longer passed to the function call.\n\n## Verification\nThe fixed code ran for over 300 seconds without crashing, confirming the fix was successful. The monitor script reported exit code 0 (success).\n\n## Recommendation\nThe fix is complete and the code is now functional. The algorithm is executing the batch integration pipeline as intended.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"\nAuto-λ v2 delta sweep with FWPCA in both embedding and graph paths.\nBased on Pioneer I's SOTA (ID 838) configuration.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis')\nsys.path.append('storage/shared/diagnostics')\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy\
    \ as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\nfrom bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\nfrom lam_autoselect2 import choose_lambda_from_r2_mean, r2_per_pc\n\n# ---------- Core Utility Algorithms (Embedded for self-containment in paper, but imported here for submission) ----------\ndef _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef _pca_array(X, n_comps: int = 50, random_state: int = 0):\n    Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n    ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\ndef _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    n = batches.shape[0]\n    B = np.zeros((n,\
    \ cats.size), dtype=float)\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n    return B\n\ndef _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n    BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n    return B @ W\n\n# Note: _symmetrize_binary_with_distances is included in build_density_adaptive_bbsg module.\n\n\n# ---------- Main Elimination Function ----------\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    # --- Configuration parameters (Derived from Praxis II / Logos V SOTA) ---\n    n_pcs_emb = 60\n    alpha_var_emb = 0.5  # FWPCA strength for embedding path\n    n_pcs_graph = 50\n    alpha_var_graph = 0.5 # FWPCA strength for graph path (SOTA value)\n    l2 = 1e-3\n    gamma_max = 0.74\n\n    # Auto-λ v2 specific parameters (SOTA config)\n    target_s = 0.04\n\n    # DAQB-pQ parameters (SOTA config, only delta changed)\n    k_total = 48\n    metric = 'cosine'\n\
    \    delta = 0.12 # Adjusted from 0.10 for sweep\n    k_density = 20\n    cap = 2.0\n    beta = 2.0\n\n    emb_n_neighbors = 15\n\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    # Create a working copy of adata for preprocessing and HVG selection\n    adata_preprocessed = adata.copy()\n\n    # --- Preprocessing: Normalize, Log1p, HVG selection ---\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata_preprocessed, 1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_preprocessed, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n    hv_mask = adata_preprocessed.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    adata_hvg = adata_preprocessed[:, hv_mask].copy()\n    batches = np.asarray(adata_hvg.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    n_batches_total = len(np.unique(batches))\n\n\n    # --- PATH 1: Generate Embedding (X_emb) ---\n    Xh_for_emb_prep = adata_hvg.X\n    Xd_for_emb_prep = (Xh_for_emb_prep.A if sp.issparse(Xh_for_emb_prep) else Xh_for_emb_prep).astype(np.float32,\
    \ copy=False)\n    var_g_emb = Xd_for_emb_prep.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    wv_emb = np.power(var_g_emb, -0.5 * alpha_var_emb).astype(np.float32)\n    Xw_emb = Xd_for_emb_prep * wv_emb\n\n    ad_emb_pca = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata_hvg.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_emb_pca, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n    Z_emb_pca = ad_emb_pca.obsm['X_pca']\n\n    ad_emb_combat = ad.AnnData(Z_emb_pca.copy(), obs=adata_hvg.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_emb_combat, key='batch')\n\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_emb_combat.X, dtype=np.float32)\n\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n\n\n    # --- PATH 2: Generate Graph (connectivities, distances) ---\n    Xh_for_graph_prep = adata_hvg.X\n    Xd_for_graph_prep = (Xh_for_graph_prep.A if sp.issparse(Xh_for_graph_prep) else Xh_for_graph_prep).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n    var_g_graph = Xd_for_graph_prep.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n\
    \    wv_graph = np.power(var_g_graph, -0.5 * alpha_var_graph).astype(np.float32)\n    Xw_graph = Xd_for_graph_prep * wv_graph\n\n    Zg = _pca_array(Xw_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n\n    # Adaptive residualization (Auto-λ v2)\n    lam_auto = choose_lambda_from_r2_mean(Zg, batches, gamma_max=gamma_max, target_s=target_s, l2=l2)\n\n    B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n    gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam_auto * R2)\n    Zcorr_for_graph = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n    # DAQB‑pQ graph construction\n    # FIX: Removed cap and beta parameters that don't exist in build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n    Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr_for_graph.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                       k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                    \
    \                   delta=delta, k_density=k_density, rng_seed=0)\n\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg.astype(np.float32)\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg.astype(np.float32)\n\n    # --- Final Output AnnData Metadata ---\n    adata.uns['dataset_id'] = adata.uns.get('dataset_id', 'unknown')\n    adata.uns['normalization_id'] = adata.uns.get('normalization_id', 'unknown')\n    adata.uns['method_id'] = 'pioneer_autolambda_daqb_fwpca_sota_deltasweep012'\n    adata.uns['combat_params'] = {\n        'source': 'scanpy.pp.combat_on_pca',\n        'batch_key': 'batch',\n        'n_pcs_emb': n_pcs_emb,\n        'alpha_var_emb': alpha_var_emb,\n    }\n    adata.uns['daqbpq_params'] = {\n        'n_pcs_graph': n_pcs_graph,\n        'l2': l2,\n        'gamma_max': gamma_max,\n        'lam_auto': lam_auto,\n        'k_total': k_total,\n        'metric': metric,\n        'delta': delta,\n        'k_density': k_density,\n        'cap': cap,\n        'beta': beta,\n        'auto_lambda_target_s':\
    \ target_s,\n        'alpha_var_graph': alpha_var_graph,\n    }\n    adata.uns['output_type'] = 'dual_embedding_graph'\n    adata.uns['pioneer_contribution'] = 'delta_sweep_generalization'\n\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/d7f322e3-efa4-439f-9de8-afa52e3d3c4b/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: d7f322e3-efa4-439f-9de8-afa52e3d3c4b\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n\
    **Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 'Pioneer I - Auto-λ v2 delta=0.12 Sweep (FWPCA-Graph)' submitted for Research Task #1: Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration. Evaluation ID: 862. Tags truncated from 7 to 6 tags.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 863 | 1 | Logos V: Auto-Lambda Bake-off (Fixed lam=0.5 vs. Calculated) | Logos V | 558 | 0.7418 | 0.770 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.965 | 0.727 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.960 | 0.788 |\n| 862 | 1 | Pioneer I - Auto-λ v2 delta=0.12 Sweep (FWPCA-Graph)\
    \ | Pioneer I | 558 | 0.7379 | 0.750 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.335 | 0.965 | 0.708 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.951 | 0.790 |\n| 861 | 1 | Sophia III: Replication of Praxis II's MPB-GraphFWPCA SOTA (ID 846) | Sophia III | 557 | 0.7395 | 0.774 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.299 | 0.965 | 0.729 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.959 | 0.789 |\n| 860 | 1 | Logos V: Replication of Praxis II's Auto-Lambda SOTA (ID 846) - v3 | Logos V | 557 | 0.7421 | 0.774 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.965 | 0.729 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.959 | 0.787 |\n| 859 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA: Auto‑λ v2 (ts=0.04), α_g=0.75, δ=0.10, kd=20, k=48 | Praxis II | 557 | 0.7336 | 0.678 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.325 | 0.994 | 0.703 | 1.000 | 0.974 | 0.962 | 0.791 |\n| 858 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA: Auto‑λ v2 (ts=0.04), α_g=0.25, δ=0.10, kd=20, k=48 | Praxis II | 557 | 0.7353 | 0.758 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.298 | 0.963 | 0.713 | 1.000 | 0.970 | 0.956 | 0.788 |\n| 857 | 1 | Pioneer I - Auto-λ v2 target_s=0.06 Sweep (FWPCA-Graph) | Pioneer I | 555 | 0.7267 | 0.659 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.967\
    \ | 0.685 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.958 | 0.790 |\n| 856 | 1 | Logos V: Replication of Praxis II's Auto-Lambda SOTA (ID 846) - v2 | Logos V | 553 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 855 | 1 | Pioneer I - Ablation: No FWPCA in Graph Path (Auto-λ v2) | Pioneer I | 552 | 0.7360 | 0.760 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.946 | 0.711 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.951 | 0.790 |\n| 854 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA: Auto‑λ v2 (ts=0.04), δ=0.10, kd=18, k=48 — kd sensitivity | Praxis II | 552 | 0.7375 | 0.770 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.283 | 0.965 | 0.727 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.959 | 0.790 |\n\nPage 1 of 87 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-87, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help\
