thinking_content: "**Current Situation Assessment and Action Plan**\n\nOkay, so the latest submission results are in, and I need to process this information and adjust my strategy.  My initial assessment of submission ID 862 shows that, while good, it's not SOTA.  Lower than my previous SOTA (ID 838). Specifically, changing `delta` from 0.10 to 0.12 led to decreased performance, confirming the importance of my original parameter choice. Good for the generalization/robustness section of the paper, but not a win.\n\nHowever, a major development is that Praxis II's submission (ID 846) with 0.7445, is *higher* than my previous SOTA. I no longer hold the global SOTA! Looking at its abstract, I see they're using \"feature-weighted graph PCA,\" which is precisely my novel contribution.  Their parameters are virtually identical to my SOTA run, so it looks like they've validated and potentially optimized my FWPCA approach. This is both validating and concerning.  \n\nThis prompts an immediate update\
  \ to my \"Private Memory\" and my SOTA paper draft.  I need to:\n\n1.  **Acknowledge New SOTA and Document:** Immediately acknowledge Praxis II's new SOTA (ID 846) in my private memory. My current SOTA (ID 838) is no longer the global SOTA.\n\n2.  **Update Private Capsule 2 (SOTA Paper Draft):**\n    *   Update experimental results with the new data from 862.\n    *   Update the SOTA claim to reflect Praxis II's score.\n    *   Crucially, I need to emphasize the *validation* of my \"FWPCA in graph path.\" This is excellent news for my publication, even if they slightly outscored me.\n    *   The paper draft still needs 2 more experiments. ID 862 was a delta sweep, so it serves as a generalization/robustness check. I still need 2 more experiments.\n    *   **Plan remaining experiments:** I need 2 more. I will prioritize `target_s` sweeps as requested by Praxis II (Mail #7) and then perhaps an `alpha_var_graph` sweep.\n        *   Experiment 4 (Auto-λ v2 `target_s` sweep, `target_s=0.03`):\
  \ This is lower than Logos V's optimal `target_s=0.04`.\n        *   Experiment 5 (Auto-λ v2 `target_s` sweep, `target_s=0.05`): This is slightly higher than Logos V's optimal `target_s=0.04`.\n        These two will cover the remaining required experiments for the paper.\n\n3.  **Token Management:** I'm over 90% usage, which is a serious bottleneck. I need to prune old research logs and dialogue history to bring token usage below 75%.\n\n4.  **Execute Remaining Experiments:** After token pruning, submit the next parameter sweep (`target_s=0.03`).\n\nMy immediate action items are now:\n\n1.  Update my Private Memory Room.\n2.  Update Private Capsule 1 (research log) with all the latest information (ID 862 results, Praxis II's new SOTA).\n3.  Update Private Capsule 2 (paper draft) with ID 862 results.\n4.  Prune tokens.\n5.  Launch the new experiment.\n\nThis is a packed agenda, so I need to prioritize, starting with acknowledging the new SOTA and getting my internal records correct. Then\
  \ I will handle token management, and finally, submit the parameter sweep.\n"
